window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["acc-27.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">حساس نقطة العمى الأيسر LBSS: لكل جانب وحدة مدمجة بالحساس، ترسل رسالة CAN لعقل الباب ليضيء مؤشر LED في المرآة.</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> تشخيص كهربائي: أكواد وخطوات فحص. الدليل 39 هو الجانب الأيمن بنفس الأسلوب.</p><div class=\"ac-chips\"><span class=\"en-chip\">B = كهرباء الجسم: 8</span><span class=\"en-chip\">U = اتصال الشبكة: 7</span></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong>كيف تقرأ كود العطل</strong><small>الرقم بعد الشرطة يدل على نوع العطل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-legend\"><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-11</b><span>قصر على الأرضي</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-12</b><span>قصر على البطارية</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-13</b><span>دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-15</b><span>قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-16</b><span>الفولتية أقل من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-17</b><span>الفولتية أعلى من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-2A</b><span>مفتاح عالق Stuck</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-84 / 85</b><span>الإشارة أقل / أعلى من المدى</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-92</b><span>أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-00</b><span>عطل عام أو بدون نوع محدد</span></div></div><p class=\"bcm-note\">الحرف الأول: B = كهرباء الجسم · C = الهيكل والحساسات · P = نقل الحركة · U = اتصال الشبكة. نفّذ دائماً الفحص المسبق Pre-Diagnostic قبل خطوات أي كود.</p></div></details></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-topic\"><summary><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">OVERVIEW</strong></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Left Blind Spot Sensor (LBSS) Module (BSM) - Electrical Diagnostics - Charger</p></div></div></details><input type=\"search\" class=\"ec-search acc-q\" placeholder=\"ابحث: كود العطل أو كلمة من الوصف\" aria-label=\"بحث\"><p class=\"bcm-note acc-cnt\">15 كود عطل. اضغط على الكود لترى شرحه.</p><div class=\"acc-list\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b128c-2a driver blind spot sensor - stuck\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B128C-2A</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER BLIND SPOT SENSOR - STUCK</small><small>العطل: عالق (Stuck)</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Blind Spot Monitor (BSM) system used in this vehicle has two control modules. One control module is dedicated to each side of the vehicle. The blind spot modules are each integral to the blind spot sensor for the same side of the vehicle. If the sensor detects a vehicle in the blind spot path, the module will send a CAN bussed message to the corresponding door module for a LED blind spot warning light request.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Left Blind Spot Sensor detects an internal failure of the radar sensor.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display SERVICE BLIND SPOT message on the cluster.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT BLIND SPOT SENSOR</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Blind Spot Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, BLIND SPOT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b128c-48 driver blind spot sensor - supervision software failure\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B128C-48</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER BLIND SPOT SENSOR - SUPERVISION SOFTWARE FAILURE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Blind Spot Monitor (BSM) system used in this vehicle has two control modules. One control module is dedicated to each side of the vehicle. The blind spot modules are each integral to the blind spot sensor for the same side of the vehicle. If the sensor detects a vehicle in the blind spot path, the module will send a CAN bussed message to the corresponding door module for a LED blind spot warning light request.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Blind Spot Sensor detects an internal failure.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) will display SERVICE BLIND SPOT message on the cluster.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>BLIND SPOT SENSOR</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Blind Spot Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, BLIND SPOT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b128c-98 driver blind spot sensor - component or system over temperature\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B128C-98</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DRIVER BLIND SPOT SENSOR - COMPONENT OR SYSTEM OVER TEMPERATURE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Blind Spot Monitor (BSM) system used in this vehicle has two control modules. One control module is dedicated to each side of the vehicle. The blind spot modules are each integral to the blind spot sensor for the same side of the vehicle. If the sensor detects a vehicle in the blind spot path, the module will send a CAN bussed message to the corresponding door module for a LED blind spot warning light request.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Blind Spot Sensor detects the internal circuit board temperature is too high.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Blind Spot System is temporarily unavailable. Mirror LEDs requested on. Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) to display BLIND SPOT TEMPORARILY UNAVAILABLE message.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>BLIND SPOT SENSOR OBSTRUCTED (MUD OR DIRT COVERING INNER FASCIA)</li><li>BLIND SPOT SENSOR</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>BLIND SPOT SENSOR</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Verify that none of the possible causes mentioned above are present. Repair as necessary.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">If none of the possible causes mentioned above are present, view repair.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Blind Spot Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, BLIND SPOT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b2199-16 battery voltage - circuit voltage below threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B2199-16</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE - CIRCUIT VOLTAGE BELOW THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أقل من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">.</p></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Engine running. Vehicle speed greater than 9.6 km/h (6 mph).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Left Blind Spot Sensor supply voltage less than 6.5 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Left Blind Spot System is temporarily unavailable. Mirror LEDs requested on. Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) to display BLIND SPOT TEMPORARILY UNAVAILABLE message.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>VEHICLE CHARGING SYSTEM</li><li>.</li><li>LEFT BLIND SPOT SENSOR</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read LBSS DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read LBSS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>VERIFY OPERATION OF THE VEHICLE CHARGING SYSTEM</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Troubleshoot any PCM charging/cranking DTCs before proceeding.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Are any charging system DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair PCM DTCs. and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Left Blind Spot Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, BLIND SPOT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b2199-17 battery voltage - circuit voltage above threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B2199-17</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE - CIRCUIT VOLTAGE ABOVE THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أعلى من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">.</p></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. Vehicle speed greater than 9.6 km/h (6 mph).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Left Blind Spot Sensor supply voltage greater than 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Blind Spot System is temporarily unavailable. Mirror LEDs requested on. Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) to display BLIND SPOT TEMPORARILY UNAVAILABLE message.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>VEHICLE CHARGING SYSTEM</li><li>.</li><li>LEFT BLIND SPOT SENSOR</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read LBSS DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read LBSS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>VERIFY OPERATION OF THE VEHICLE CHARGING SYSTEM</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Troubleshoot any PCM charging/cranking DTCs before proceeding.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery is fully charged.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Are any charging system DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair PCM DTCs. and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Left Blind Spot Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, BLIND SPOT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b223b-00 vehicle configuration mismatch\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B223B-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">VEHICLE CONFIGURATION MISMATCH</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Blind Spot Monitor (BSM) system used in this vehicle has two control modules. One control module is dedicated to each side of the vehicle. The blind spot modules are each integral to the blind spot sensor for the same side of the vehicle. If the sensor detects a vehicle in the blind spot path, the module will send a CAN .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">bussed message to the corresponding door module for a LED blind spot warning light request.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This DTC will set if the vehicle type is not identified or incorrectly identified.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>INCORRECT VEHICLE CONFIGURATION IN THE BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read LBSS DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Record the Environmental Data.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read LBSS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Verify the correct vehicle configuration in the BCM. If the vehicle configuration is incorrect, perform a restore vehicle configuration.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Use the scan tool to read DTCs in all other modules. If any communication DTCs are present, perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Perform any Technical Service Bulletins that apply. If no problems are found, test is complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b2598-00 door module front left\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B2598-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DOOR MODULE FRONT LEFT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Blind Spot Monitor (BSM) system used in this vehicle has two control modules. One control module is dedicated to each side of the vehicle. The blind spot modules are each integral to the blind spot sensor for the same side of the vehicle. If the sensor detects a vehicle in the blind spot path, the module will send a CAN bussed message to the corresponding door module for a LED blind spot warning light request.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. Vehicle speed greater than 6 mph (9.6 km/h).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Driver&#x27;s Door Module (DDM) is reporting a DTC over the CAN bus.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Blind Spot System is temporarily unavailable. Mirror LEDs requested on. Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) to display BLIND SPOT TEMPORARILY UNAVAILABLE message.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DTC IN DRIVERS DOOR MODULE (DDM)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read LBSS DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read LBSS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension. Repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b2599-00 door module front right\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B2599-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">DOOR MODULE FRONT RIGHT</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Blind Spot Monitor (BSM) system used in this vehicle has two control modules. One control module is</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">dedicated to each side of the vehicle. The blind spot modules are each integral to the blind spot sensor for the same side of the vehicle. If the sensor detects a vehicle in the blind spot path, the module will send a CAN bussed message to the corresponding door module for a LED blind spot warning light request.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on. Vehicle speed greater than 6 mph (9.6 km/h).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Passenger Door Module is reporting a DTC over the CAN bus.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Blind Spot System is temporarily unavailable. Mirror LEDs requested on. Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) to display BLIND SPOT TEMPORARILY UNAVAILABLE message.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>DTC IN PASSENGER DOOR MODULE (PDM)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read LBSS DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read LBSS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DIAGNOSTIC CODE INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension. Repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0011-00 can interior bus off performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0011-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CAN INTERIOR BUS OFF PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">.</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For an in-depth explanation of the CAN system operation, refer to DESCRIPTION .</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. Battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CAN IHS bus has experienced a failure due to a circuit or processor fault.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>OPEN OR SHORTED CAN IHS BUS CIRCUIT</li><li>CAN IHS RELATED MODULE</li><li>CAN IHS RELATED STAR CONNECTOR (IF EQUIPPED)</li><li>CAN IHS RELATED SPLICE BLOCK CONNECTOR (IF EQUIPPED)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the scan tool will not communicate with CAN IHS, proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS .</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, run a Vehicle Scan Report and attached it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the Vehicle Scan Report, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ATTEMPT TO LOCATE AN INTERMITTENT CIRCUIT FAULT</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">.</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The scan tool LOSS OF COMM TEST will force the modules on the CAN IHS bus to continuously ping each other.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, initiate the LOSS OF COMM TEST.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A value above 0 under the NUMBER OF NO RESPONSES can help indicate the location of a circuit fault while wiggling the related CAN IHS bus circuits.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The scan tool lag time between pings is almost 1 full second. Keep this in mind while wiggling the wires and connectors.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>In a systematic manner, wiggle the applicable CAN IHS circuits at each related module, in-line connector, and Star/Splice Block Connector (if equipped) while monitoring the NUMBER OF NO RESPONSES on the scan tool.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the above test help locate the fault?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>PERFORM VISUAL INSPECTION OF CONNECTORS, TERMINALS AND WIRES</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all CAN IHS related module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect the harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Connect all CAN IHS related module harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged. .</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Using the Vehicle Scan Report, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">The conditions that caused this DTC to set are no longer present. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0100-00 lost communication with ecm/pcm\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0100-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH ECM/PCM</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع ECM/PCM</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0140-00 lost communication with body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0140-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0203-00 lost communication with left front door module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0203-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH LEFT FRONT DOOR MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع LEFT FRONT DOOR MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0204-00 lost communication with right front door module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0204-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH RIGHT FRONT DOOR MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع RIGHT FRONT DOOR MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1194-01 lost communication with passenger side blind spot sensor - general\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1194-01</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH PASSENGER SIDE BLIND SPOT SENSOR - GENERAL</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع PASSENGER SIDE BLIND SPOT SENSOR - GENERAL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">ELECTRICAL FAILURE</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">.</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Blind Spot Monitor (BSM) system used in this vehicle has two control modules. One control module is dedicated to each side of the vehicle. The blind spot modules are each integral to the blind spot sensor for the same side of the vehicle. If the sensor detects a vehicle in the blind spot path, the module will send a CAN bussed message to the corresponding door module for a LED blind spot warning light request.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Left Blind Spot Sensor (LBSS) does not receive messages from the Right Blind Spot Sensor (RBSS).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RUN RELAY OUTPUT OPEN</li><li>GROUND CIRCUIT(S) OPEN</li><li>CAN IHS BUS CIRCUIT(S) OPEN</li><li>.</li><li>RIGHT BLIND SPOT SENSOR (RBSS)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLE CODE (DTC)</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool display this DTC as active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition that caused this code to set is not present at this time. Check for an intermittent condition by inspecting the related wiring harness for chafed, pierced, pinched, and partially broken wires. Also inspect the related connectors for broken, bent, pushed out, spread, corroded, or contaminated terminals.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>(F923) RUN RELAY CIRCUIT OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Right Blind Spot Sensor (RBSS) harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (F923) RUN RELAY OUTPUT circuit at the RBSS harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (F923) RUN RELAY OUTPUT circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>(Z922) GROUND CIRCUIT(S) OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, back probe the (Z922) ground circuits at the RBSS harness connector. (Do not back probe sealed connectors.)</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z922) ground circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D264) AND (D265) CAN IHS BUS CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D264) CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit between the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C4 harness connector and the RBSS harness connector</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D265) CAN IHS Bus (+) circuit between the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C4 harness connector and the RBSS harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Blind Spot Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, BLIND SPOT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D265) or (D264) CAN IHS Bus circuit for an open. Inspect the connector for damage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u1194-87 lost communication with passenger side blind spot sensor - missing\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U1194-87</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH PASSENGER SIDE BLIND SPOT SENSOR - MISSING</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع PASSENGER SIDE BLIND SPOT SENSOR - MISSING</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">MESSAGE</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">.</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Blind Spot Monitor (BSM) system used in this vehicle has two control modules. One control module is dedicated to each side of the vehicle. The blind spot modules are each integral to the blind spot sensor for the same side of the vehicle. If the sensor detects a vehicle in the blind spot path, the module will send a CAN bussed message to the corresponding door module for a LED blind spot warning light request.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Left Blind Spot Sensor (LBSS) does not receive messages from the Right Blind Spot Sensor (RBSS).</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Blind Spot System is temporarily unavailable. Mirror LEDs requested on. Electronic Vehicle Information Center (EVIC) to display BLIND SPOT TEMPORARILY UNAVAILABLE message. .</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RUN RELAY CONTROL CIRCUIT OPEN OR SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>GROUND CIRCUIT(S) OPEN</li><li>CAN IHS BUS CIRCUIT(S) OPEN</li><li>RIGHT BLIND SPOT SENSOR (RBSS)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read LBSS DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the recorded Environmental Data, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read LBSS DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension and repair as necessary. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>(F923) RUN RELAY OUTPUT CIRCUIT OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Left Blind Spot Sensor (RBSS) harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, back probe the (F923) RUN RELAY OUTPUT circuit at the RBSS harness connector. (Do not back probe sealed connectors.)</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (F923) RUN RELAY OUTPUT circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>(Z922) GROUND CIRCUIT(S) OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z922) Ground circuit at the RBSS harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z922) Ground circuit(s) for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (D264) AND (D265) CAN IHS BUS CIRCUITS FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D264) CAN IHS Bus (-) circuit between the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C4 harness connector and the RBSS harness connector</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (D265) CAN IHS Bus (+) circuit between the Rear CAN IHS Star Connector C4 harness connector and the RBSS harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is resistance below 3.0 Ohms on both circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Blind Spot Sensor in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SENSOR, BLIND SPOT, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (D265) or (D264) CAN IHS Bus circuit for an open. Inspect the connector for damage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910331</p></div></div></details></div></details></div>";
